{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Do not eat of it na.</b> If an Egyptian comes into your houses at the time of its roasting, do not remove it from the fire, saying 'it is well roasted' and it is still <b>נא</b> — and all this you would say out of fear; therefore it was said: do not fear them." "<b>And boiled in broth</b> etc. According to its plain sense, the vav of <b>ובשל</b> is superfluous, and this is what it says: I ask of you, do not eat it boiled in water, lest it appear a hidden matter, but rather roasted by fire in the open." "<b>Na.</b> An expression of request." "<b>Its head on its legs and on its innards.</b> With its legs and with its innards. A model: 'upon the field of the land it shall be reckoned.' The men upon the women — that is, even at the time of roasting, entirely whole, so that it be visible that it is from their fear."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:08.148885479Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}